🔧 Part 1: Setting Up a Local Endpoint on a Cluster
Step 1: Download Globus Connect Personal
bash
# Download the latest version for Linux
wget https://downloads.globus.org/globus-connect-personal/stable/globusconnectpersonal-latest.tgz

# Extract the archive
tar -xzf globusconnectpersonal-latest.tgz
cd globusconnectpersonal-*
Step 2: Register Your Endpoint
bash
# Run the setup (this opens a browser for authentication)
./globusconnectpersonal -setup

# Follow the browser prompts to log in with your email
# After successful setup, you'll see:
# "registered new endpoint, id: YOUR-ENDPOINT-UUID"
Step 3: Configure Accessible Paths
bash
# Stop the service if running
./globusconnectpersonal -stop

# Edit the paths configuration file
nano ~/.globusonline/lta/config-paths

# Add your working directories (one per line)
# Format: /full/path/to/directory,0,1
# Example:
/mnt/shared/scratch/zchen/,0,1
/mnt/shared/projects/rbge/Data_download/Globus/,0,1

# Save and exit
Step 4: Start the Service
bash
# Start in background mode
./globusconnectpersonal -start &

# Check status
./globusconnectpersonal -status
# Should show: "Globus Online: connected"
